  "text": {
    "intro": "Mr Halloran repairs clocks. Those on the bench are all insisting on a different hour.\nFive clocks are involved. Determine each clock's shelf, owner, fault and chime.\n- **Clock**: a ship's chronometer, a carriage clock, a longcase clock, a cuckoo clock and an anniversary clock.\n- **Shelf** (listed from lower to higher): the bottom shelf, the second shelf, the third shelf, the fourth shelf and the fifth shelf.\n- **Owner**: Mr Dziedzic, Dr Vasquez, Father Brennan, Ms Trevino and Mrs Oyelaran.\n- **Fault**: a bent pendulum rod, a snapped mainspring, a cracked suspension spring, a gummed-up pivot and a worn escape wheel.\n- **Chime**: Westminster; a single strike; no chime at all; a ship's bell; and a bell and gong.\nEvery clock has a different shelf, owner, fault and chime, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The clock that suffers from a bent pendulum rod sits on the third shelf. The clock that suffers from a snapped mainspring is lower than the third shelf in shelf order.",
      "The clock that sounds no chime at all sits on the second shelf.",
      "The clock that belongs to Dr Vasquez and the fourth shelf are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other.",
      "A cuckoo clock sits on the second shelf.",
      "The clock that sounds a ship's bell falls somewhere between the clock that suffers from a gummed-up pivot and the fourth shelf in shelf order, matching neither.",
      "The clock that sounds a single strike is exactly one shelf lower than the clock that belongs to Mr Dziedzic, with no shelf in between.",
      "The clock that sounds Westminster and the clock that suffers from a worn escape wheel are exactly four shelves apart in shelf order.",
      "The clock that suffers from a snapped mainspring and the clock that belongs to Ms Trevino are exactly two shelves apart in shelf order.",
      "The clock that suffers from a snapped mainspring falls somewhere between an anniversary clock and the clock that belongs to Mr Dziedzic in shelf order, matching neither.",
      "A carriage clock is lower than the clock that sounds a single strike in shelf order.",
      "A longcase clock and the clock that belongs to Father Brennan are exactly four shelves apart in shelf order."
    ]
  }
